                <pb facs="0317" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg211"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan reports that he has advised Capt. Schley to tender evidence in
                    accordance with the telegraphic instructions of November 1, and that the United
                    States consul at Valparaiso reports that the same judge who would not allow an
                    officer of the Baltimore/to be present permitted the secretary of the German
                    consulate to attend the investigation of the killing of a German man-of-war’s
                    man, which took place last month.</p>
            </div>
